# The three places a translation counts once something the model mentions twice. One row per
# elimination: the sum before, the overlap, and what names the overlap.
#
# Each overlap is named by a relation, not filed
#   Each is a sum less an overlap, and the overlap is a filed number nowhere here: the overlap of
#   two lane sets is the set of layers, the overlap of many part references is the document, and the
#   overlap of three buffers is the layer they are substitutes within. Each is a relation with a
#   name, which is the test that made `eliminations/derived.sqlc` possible. A translation that could
#   not name its overlap would have to file one, and nothing in BPMN could hold it.
#
# The first is the model's, not the emitter's
#   It is the one worth knowing. `pm.draw` has no `buffer` column, so a draw is against a layer and
#   never against one of its three buffers. The model already made that elimination, on the ground
#   that the buffers are substitutes (`layers/absorption.sqlc`), and every diagram inherits it. The
#   buffer missing from the draws' key is the elimination.
#
# A fourth would be unsound
#   That is why it is not on this list. Dropping a part's lane membership would count each call once
#   instead of once as a node and once as a placement, but the overlap there cannot be worked out: a
#   call outside a lane has lost which layer it feeds, so what remains says only that there is
#   nesting here, which is what a subProcess already is. That would eliminate the composed end of
#   each part, and `diagrams/lane_membership.sqlc` refuses it.
-- the derived overlaps a BPMN emission takes, each against the relation that names it.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('the buffer',   'a draw for every operation, layer and buffer',
                   'the layer, within which the three engines are substitutes',
                   'layers/absorption.sqlc'),
  ('the lane set', 'a lane for every layer drawn on and another for every layer induced into',
                   'the layer set, enumerated twice over one conformed dimension',
                   'diagrams/lane_grain.sqlc'),
  ('the import',   'one per cross-document part',  'the document, referenced many times from one filing',
                   'diagrams/cross_document.sqlc')
) AS e(elimination, the_sum, the_overlap, named_by)
